    "durationMs": 240262,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully verified. \n\n**What was built:**\n- `app/` — async FastAPI app with SQLAlchemy 2 (psycopg 3 driver) reading `DATABASE_URL` from the environment via pydantic-settings\n- `alembic/` + `alembic.ini` — migration creating the `links` table (unique indexed code, url, clicks, created_at); `start.sh` runs `alembic upgrade head` before serving\n- `start.sh` — applies migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (verified working from any cwd, no installs inside)\n- `tests/test_api.py` — 24 integration tests that boot the real server via `start.sh`\n- `README.md` — startup instructions and endpoint reference\n\n**Verification results:**\n- All 24 tests pass: create (custom/generated codes), duplicate 409, invalid/missing URLs and codes 422, malformed JSON 422, all errors returning JSON with an `error` field\n- `GET /r/{code}` returns 302 with the exact stored `Location` and increments clicks once per request (atomic `UPDATE ... clicks + 1 ... RETURNING`)\n- `GET /links` returns `{\"items\", \"total\"}` in ascending creation order\n- URLs are returned byte-for-byte unchanged (no trailing-slash normalization), localhost URLs accepted\n- Restart persistence confirmed: killed the server, restarted, click count and data survived\n\nOne extra dependency was needed — `greenlet` (required by SQLAlchemy's async mode, absent from the stack pins) — installed and committed to `requirements.txt`. The database was left pristine (test rows deleted, schema intact) and no servers are running."
